\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Information available around the December 25, 2022 forecast origin, spanning November 27, 2022 through January 22, 2023 on the $\qopname  \relax o{log}(1+x)$ scale with $x$ in m$^3$/s. Before the origin, the panel shows USGS observations and the NWS and GloFAS retrospective products used for source-discrepancy learning; after the origin, it shows held-out USGS verification together with the operational NWS and GloFAS forecast ensembles. Horizontal dashed lines show approximate current-rating discharge equivalents of the current NWS minor and major stage categories at BTEC1/USGS 11160500. These levels provide magnitude references on the discharge scale. \relax }}{5}{figure.caption.3}}
\newlabel{fig:ensembles}{{2}{5}{Information available around the December 25, 2022 forecast origin, spanning November 27, 2022 through January 22, 2023 on the $\log (1+x)$ scale with $x$ in m$^3$/s. Before the origin, the panel shows USGS observations and the NWS and GloFAS retrospective products used for source-discrepancy learning; after the origin, it shows held-out USGS verification together with the operational NWS and GloFAS forecast ensembles. Horizontal dashed lines show approximate current-rating discharge equivalents of the current NWS minor and major stage categories at BTEC1/USGS 11160500. These levels provide magnitude references on the discharge scale. \relax }{figure.caption.3}{}}
