\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Empirical quantile reliability across the five forecast origins, separately for eight-day and 28-day horizons. Curves show the frequency of observations at or below each predictive quantile for exAL-M-T1 and the raw-product, EMOS and seasonal references; the diagonal marks the nominal probability. Raw NWS is available over eight days. The legend labels RAW-GLOFAS and RAW-NWS identify the raw ensembles, EMOS-GLOFAS identifies the GloFAS EMOS correction, and CLIM-SEASONAL identifies seasonal climatology. Strict frequencies and exact ties are reported in the supplementary results. These descriptive curves pool 40 and 140 cases, respectively.\relax }}{17}{figure.caption.16}}
\newlabel{fig:no_refit_reliability}{{4}{17}{Empirical quantile reliability across the five forecast origins, separately for eight-day and 28-day horizons. Curves show the frequency of observations at or below each predictive quantile for exAL-M-T1 and the raw-product, EMOS and seasonal references; the diagonal marks the nominal probability. Raw NWS is available over eight days. The legend labels RAW-GLOFAS and RAW-NWS identify the raw ensembles, EMOS-GLOFAS identifies the GloFAS EMOS correction, and CLIM-SEASONAL identifies seasonal climatology. Strict frequencies and exact ties are reported in the supplementary results. These descriptive curves pool 40 and 140 cases, respectively.\relax }{figure.caption.16}{}}
